# Reproducibility Packet — its own ignore rules.
#
# This file exists so the packet folder stays correct when it is copied out on
# its own and tracked separately. It is intentionally narrower than a whole
# project's ignore file: everything a reader needs to reproduce a result is
# meant to be tracked here.

# Virtual environments created by the setup step in README.md
.venv/
venv/

# Python bytecode and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Recording data and sorter output. Nothing in this packet downloads these, but
# a reader who fetches the dandiset locally will land them next to the scripts.
*.nwb
*.dat
*.bin
*.zarr/
sorter_output/
kilosort4/
.kilosort/
phy/

# Large rebuildable arrays
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5

# Logs and OS noise
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Deliberately NOT ignored — do not add a rule that catches these:
#
#   results/*.txt, results/*.json     the recorded reports and their inputs
#   results/templates_snapshot_*.csv  the pinned upstream donor table (~2 MB),
#                                     which is what makes offline replay
#                                     byte-for-byte rather than approximate
#   results/dandi_000409_assets.json  the archive asset listing (~0.7 MB)
#   results/*_index.jsonl             resumable per-asset survey indexes
#   results/ccf_label_map_derived_records.json
#                                     the per-asset votes that let the label
#                                     map be rebuilt with no network reads
#   scripts/utils/ccf_label_map_derived.json
#                                     the derived map itself, imported at run
#                                     time rather than regenerated
#
# The upstream sources these came from are mutable, so "re-download it" is not
# equivalent to having the pinned copy.
